    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Shang clan city chapters do not name a cultivation path for this Gu. Path talk in those chapters attaches to Li Hao (strength path background, later support style), not to the toad’s own classification.",
        "chapters": [
          290
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
  "appearance": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "It is a giant toad, larger than a mammoth, with two eyes as large as stone mills. Its body is grey, with a huge stomach and strong limbs. There is green moss on its skin, and even some tiny rocks on the surface. Its back is extremely swollen, like it is carrying a small hill. That hill is real, made of mountain rocks about ten and a half feet high, with many layers and folds, like it is shaved by swords and axes. Grass and weed grow on the mountain rocks, and there are two or three trees.",
        "chapters": [
          289
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "It is heavy and cumbersome. The hill on its back is made of dense mountain rocks, and once its four legs stand on the ground it is like an unmovable mountain. The text ranks it among the heaviest rank three Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          289
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Spectators compare it to a castle that combines attack and defense, with low speed as its only clear weakness.",
        "chapters": [
          289
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "No cited chapter gives a Chinese name, glyph, or feed.",
        "chapters": [],
        "certainty": "inferred",
        "confidence": "C",
        "verification": "no_citation",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ],
    "visual_confidence": "text_described"
  },
  "abilities": {
    "activation_raw": null,
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Its signature move is to leap up and crash down like a mountain, hard enough to shake a battle stage and knock spectators off balance.",
        "chapters": [
          289
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Li Hao also rides it into a ground charge that can send a foe flying if it connects.",
        "chapters": [
          290
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Its defense is high enough that early blows from Fang Yuan’s beast-phantom strikes only make it sway, and onlookers treat it as a lofty, immovable image,",
        "chapters": [
          290
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "until sustained all-out attacks force it to croak, spit blood, and finally die when the hill on its back collapses.",
        "chapters": [
          291
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan beats the mountain back toad to death on the stage; the hill on its back collapses under his final punch, and Li Hao dies in the same fight.",
        "chapters": [
          291
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "fate-on-the-battle-stage",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "He does not refine or keep the toad: it is already dead, and he gains other Gu from the match instead.",
        "chapters": [
          293
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "fate-on-the-battle-stage",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
